// ============================================================
// HIGH-YIELD "WHEN DO I USE WHAT?"
// ============================================================

// mvn -version
// -> Check Maven installation and which Java Maven uses.

// mvn clean install
// -> Normal full Maven build/install.

// mvn clean install -DskipTests
// -> Build/package while temporarily skipping test execution.

// mvn dependency:tree
// -> Investigate dependency/version conflicts.

// mvn clean install -U
// -> Force Maven to check updated dependencies.

// mvn clean install -e
// -> Get detailed Maven error information.

// mvn clean install -X
// -> Get very detailed/debug Maven output.

// git status
// -> See current Git state.

// git diff
// -> See unstaged changes.

// git add .
// -> Stage changes.

// git commit
// -> Save staged changes as a commit.

// git revert
// -> Undo a committed change while preserving history.

// git restore --staged
// -> Unstage a file without deleting it.

// git stash
// -> Temporarily store unfinished changes.

// git stash pop
// -> Restore stashed changes.

// git rebase main
// -> Put feature work on top of latest main for a cleaner history.

// git reflog
// -> Find/recover commits or previous HEAD positions.

// git remote add origin
// -> Connect local repository to a remote repository.

// git push
// -> Upload local commits to remote repository.

// docker build
// -> Create an image.

// docker run
// -> Create/start a container from an image.

// docker ps
// -> See running containers.

// docker ps -a
// -> See all containers, including stopped ones.

// docker logs
// -> Diagnose container/application startup problems.

// -p 8080:8080
// -> Map host port 8080 to container port 8080.

// docker login
// -> Authenticate to DockerHub.

// docker tag
// -> Give an image a DockerHub repository/tag name.

// docker push
// -> Upload image to DockerHub.

// ============================================================
// LAST-MINUTE EXAM RULES
// ============================================================

// 1. Do not panic if Maven gives an error.
//    Read the FIRST meaningful ERROR.

// 2. Do not assume BUILD SUCCESS means the web application is running.
//    Check server startup and port.

// 3. Do not confuse an image with a container:
//    docker build -> image
//    docker run   -> container

// 4. Do not confuse Git staging and committing:
//    git add -> staging
//    git commit -> repository

// 5. For "undo commit but preserve history":
//    git revert

// 6. For "temporarily save unfinished changes":
//    git stash

// 7. For "recover lost commit":
//    git reflog

// 8. For "dependency conflict":
//    mvn dependency:tree

// 9. For "mvn not recognized":
//    install/configure Maven and PATH.

// 10. For Docker port mapping:
//     HOST:CONTAINER

// 11. Make sure the Dockerfile is named exactly:
//     Dockerfile
//     NOT Dockerfile.txt

// 12. Use the actual JAR/WAR filename produced under target/.

// 13. Use the Java version required by the actual HMS project rather than blindly changing it.

